  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Find all three-digit numbers (in base 10) that are 13 times the sum of their digits.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$117,156,195$.\n\nWrite the number as $100a+10b+c$ and use the digit bounds.",
      "worked": "Let the hundreds, tens and units digits be $a,b,c$, with $1\\le a\\le9$ and $0\\le b,c\\le9$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}100a+10b+c&=13(a+b+c)\\\\87a&=3b+12c\\\\29a&=b+4c.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $b+4c\\le45$, the hundreds digit must be $a=1$. Thus $b+4c=29$. The digit bounds give $5\\le c\\le7$, so $(b,c)=(9,5),(5,6),(1,7)$.\n\nThe numbers are $117,156,195$. Checking:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}117&=13(1+1+7)\\\\156&=13(1+5+6)\\\\195&=13(1+9+5).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
